 "citation": "Kerala Antimicrobial Resistance Surveillance Network (KARS-Net). Annual Report 2025 (Data from 1 January to 31 December 2024). Thiruvananthapuram: Department of Microbiology, Government Medical College, Thiruvananthapuram (state nodal centre), Kerala Antimicrobial Resistance Strategic Action Plan (KARSAP), Department of Health Services, Kerala; 2025.",
 "reporting": "Percent resistant by pathogen and specimen (blood, pus aspirate, other sterile body fluids, urine; stool for Salmonella, Shigella and Vibrio cholerae), all location types pooled, with number tested and number resistant; blood isolates also charted by location type (OPD, IPD, ICU) with printed data labels; MRSA and VRE yearly trend charts.",
 "method": "WHONET collation and analysis; CLSI interpretive criteria; disc diffusion, broth microdilution and automated AST at the sites; colistin by broth microdilution or agar dilution per the NARS-Net SOP 2023; first isolate per patient, specimen type and pathogen (62,087 isolates reported, 55,640 unique-patient isolates). Percentages not computed when fewer than 30 isolates were tested.",
 "measure": "R",
 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Tables 4 to 6 and 8 to 12 parsed from the PDF text layer (pdfplumber words assigned to columns by x position); Table 7 (Klebsiella) entered from the page image because its pus aspirate cells are vertically offset. Every value compared by eye with the pages rendered at scale 2.2, and every printed percentage recomputed from its printed counts (one disagreement recorded as a conflict). Location charts: Figures 7, 8 and 12 are images and were read from the rendered pages; Figures 10 and 11 have a text layer whose labels were matched to bars by position and legend colour (OPD grey, IPD orange, ICU blue) on scale-4 crops, the text statement for Pseudomonas ceftazidime (ICU 38%, IPD 32%, OPD 37%) confirming the order. Trend charts (images) read from the rendered pages. Count Tables 2 and 3 checked against the images and their printed totals. Page numbers are 1-based PDF pages."
 },
 "notes": "Kerala state antibiogram (KARS-Net Annual Report 2025), data from 1 January to 31 December 2024: 47 laboratories in 13 districts. All figures are percent resistant (intermediate counted as not resistant). Specimen PA (pus aspirate) is recorded as pus and OSBF (other sterile body fluids) as sterile. The specimen tables pool all location types (set all); blood rows by location (OPD, IPD, ICU) come from the bar charts. The Salmonella table covers blood and stool isolates together (recorded as all specimens). The all-specimen S. aureus (cefoxitin) and Enterococcus (vancomycin) rows carry the MRSA and VRE yearly trends. Drugs printed \"-\" (fewer than 30 tested) are left out.",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: 109 of 435 cells (seeded 25% sample over all 15 tables and charts), all 43 row n values and all 54 counts read from the page images (scale 2.5 to 5, the dense Figure 10 cropped into halves) before comparing with the extraction: 0 transcription errors; organism, specimen and OPD/IPD/ICU setting correct on every sampled row.",
  "Whole-file cross-checks: an independent word-position parse of Tables 4 to 12 (rows taken from the ruling lines, so the raised pus aspirate cells of Table 7 and the raised S. Paratyphi % column of Table 8 fall in the right rows) matched all 277 printed percentages and every number tested; all 156 blood location values match Figures 7, 8, 10, 11 and 12, with every label on the bar of its drug and location (vector bar geometry for Figures 10 and 11, measured bar lengths on the rendered images for Figures 7, 8 and 12; no label disagrees with its bar). MRSA and VRE trend labels confirmed.",
  "Conflict confirmed accurate: Acinetobacter urine ceftazidime printed 57% resistant but 231 of 507 = 46%. The only other printed percentage that its counts do not give is S. Typhi ceftriaxone 2% (1 of 68 = 1.5%), under 1 point and already noted on the row. Figure 9 (E. coli blood by location) is absent from the PDF (caption only), as the extraction says.",
  "Lead 2026-09-26: \"PA (pus aspirate)\" (NCDC SOP category, aspirated pus, swabs excluded) filed under specimen \"deep\" (deep infections, aspirates), as for NARS-Net, TARS-Net and AARSNET; 6 rows and 6 counts moved from \"pus\"."
 ],
